WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.260
Amazon's cloud is largely sold out through 2027, pinning AI labs to capacity already booked.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:13.240
This is MAG 7 Daily, episode 32. After that booking, google's ad line, apple's evidence

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:19.080
fight, and shuttered french stores, then the counterpoint, aerobotaxi thread, and the calendar.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:25.240
Andy Jassy said Friday on a video podcast with Andreson Horowitz co-founder Ben Horowitz,

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:31.300
and General Partner Eric Tornberg, that Amazon cannot keep up with AI labs and enterprises.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:37.840
He said 2026 capacity is already sold out, and a good chunk of 2028 is committed to.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:44.680
Amazon reports third quarter results on October 29. Earlier this year, the company put 2026

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:51.160
capital spending at about $220 billion. Jassy added that Amazon could invest a lot more,

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.700
and that it would not be a bad use of capital.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:56.260
Yesterday, the spend race was the story.

00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:58.700
Today, the capacity those dollars buy

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.520
is what he says is already booked.

00:01:01.675 --> 00:01:04.635
Google rewrote a privacy line on October 16th.

00:01:05.175 --> 00:01:06.995
The old text said personalized ads

00:01:06.995 --> 00:01:10.175
were not based on drive, Gmail, or photos content.

00:01:10.955 --> 00:01:12.795
RS Technica reports the new sentence

00:01:12.795 --> 00:01:15.255
keeps that limit only unless a person chooses

00:01:15.255 --> 00:01:17.535
to share that data with other Google services

00:01:17.535 --> 00:01:19.335
that support personalized ads.

00:01:19.335 --> 00:01:25.415
Turning on personal intelligence, out since early 2026, is the switch that hands several

00:01:25.415 --> 00:01:27.615
apps' data to Google's AI products.

00:01:28.235 --> 00:01:32.915
The policy's own example says search may use data a person allows it to see in order

00:01:32.915 --> 00:01:35.515
to personalize content, including ads.

00:01:36.115 --> 00:01:41.055
Personal intelligence stays opt-in, and Google still says advertisers do not get a name

00:01:41.055 --> 00:01:42.795
or email address without permission.

00:01:43.851 --> 00:01:48.971
Apple and the U.S. Department of Justice are split in a filing this week over how recent

00:01:48.971 --> 00:01:55.351
the documents in their antitrust case must be. They had agreed to a June 20th, 2025 cutoff.

00:01:55.991 --> 00:02:01.951
Evidence gathering now runs to late May 2027, and department lawyers want records created up to

00:02:01.951 --> 00:02:08.211
30 days before that end, to test whether the alleged conduct is still going. Apple says widening

00:02:08.211 --> 00:02:13.131
the search would push the case back several months. The company says it has already reviewed more

00:02:13.131 --> 00:02:17.971
than 11 million documents and produce more than 2 million spanning 18 years.

00:02:18.591 --> 00:02:24.191
The case filed in March 2024 accuses Apple of illegally guarding a smartphone monopoly

00:02:24.191 --> 00:02:27.171
by limiting rival apps, services, and devices.

00:02:27.771 --> 00:02:28.971
Apple denies that.

00:02:29.511 --> 00:02:33.691
The filing asks the court to note that the two sides cannot fix the document fight on

00:02:33.691 --> 00:02:34.091
their own.

00:02:35.083 --> 00:02:39.403
Seven Apple stores in France are shut today, before another round of demonstrations.

00:02:39.403 --> 00:02:44.283
Mac rumors, citing Mac Generation, names all three Paris locations,

00:02:44.623 --> 00:02:49.603
Shams Alize, Opera, and Marshae, Saint Germain, plus Bordeaux, Saint Catherine,

00:02:50.343 --> 00:02:52.763
Lille, Strasbourg, and Exome Provence.

00:02:53.323 --> 00:02:54.803
Those seven open onto the street.

00:02:55.403 --> 00:02:57.203
Mall stores were expected to stay open.

00:02:57.903 --> 00:03:00.363
Looters hit Lille and Bordeaux on October 17,

00:03:01.003 --> 00:03:02.403
along with many other businesses.

00:03:03.043 --> 00:03:07.063
The Associated Press said the protests are about living costs and school conditions.

00:03:07.063 --> 00:03:10.083
hundreds of thousands marched peacefully that day.

00:03:10.663 --> 00:03:12.823
Violence and looting broke out in several cities.

00:03:13.303 --> 00:03:18.063
Afterward, reports described stolen iPhones flashing warnings that they were disabled and

00:03:18.063 --> 00:03:21.943
being tracked, with instructions to take them back to the store they came from.

00:03:22.563 --> 00:03:25.803
List signal posted a video that purportedly shows the message.

00:03:26.715 --> 00:03:34.715
The UK put 100 million pounds, reported as $134 million, into an AI Biosecurity Lab backed

00:03:34.715 --> 00:03:41.015
by OpenAI, Anthropic, and Google Deep Mind. Bloomberg cast the lab as one piece of a wider

00:03:41.015 --> 00:03:44.495
effort to help the government see and handle risks from the technology.

00:03:45.572 --> 00:03:50.212
Helen Chiang is leaving Microsoft, an internal Xbox memo seen by the Verge says.

00:03:50.872 --> 00:03:55.792
She was the division's first chief operating officer, a job created only a few months ago.

00:03:56.192 --> 00:04:00.492
She spent 21 years at the company and ran Minecraft before the Xbox role.

00:04:00.492 --> 00:04:03.052
The memo says today is her last day.

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:09.190
The Financial Times frames a proposed Tesla Space X merger as a wager that goes all in

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:09.750
on AI.

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:14.310
A Bloomberg run down the same day said Elon Musk wants that combination.

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:19.610
What cuts against reading Amazon's cloud as fully closed is chassis's own caveat.

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:25.330
He said the company always holds some capacity back for on-demand use, for bedrock, or

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:28.610
for EC2, and that the sold out part is the big chunks.

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:31.930
EC2 is the service that rents cloud servers.

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:36.030
Bedrock is how customers reach AI models to build generative apps.

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:38.350
He never sighs that leftover slice.

00:04:38.930 --> 00:04:42.010
Set next to the $220 billion already planned.

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:46.690
His remark that more spending would not be a bad use of capital is the open question.

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:50.210
The stated check does not on his account finish the demand.

00:04:51.353 --> 00:04:56.613
Waymo and Tesla are the two robotaxi bets trading key lines up, and Waymo's paid book

00:04:56.613 --> 00:04:58.213
is the number that separates them.

00:04:58.213 --> 00:05:04.873
time. By March 2026, weekly paid driverless orders were about 500,000. Waymo belongs to

00:05:04.873 --> 00:05:10.153
Google parent Alphabet. Service or deployment already reaches 10 major U.S. cities, and

00:05:10.153 --> 00:05:15.173
the company wants to push toward 1 million weekly orders by the end of the year. A driverless

00:05:15.173 --> 00:05:21.033
ride-hailing service in Toronto is planned for 2028, the first Canadian market. Cars go

00:05:21.033 --> 00:05:24.413
on to local roads soon for manually driven mapping and testing.

00:05:24.413 --> 00:05:29.573
Eleament fleet management takes fleet maintenance, customer service, and daily operations.

00:05:30.213 --> 00:05:35.053
Passenger service still needs local approval, and the testing sits in Ontario's automated

00:05:35.053 --> 00:05:36.473
vehicle pilot program.

00:05:37.113 --> 00:05:41.913
Toronto is also the weather exam, ice, snow, cold, and dense city traffic.

00:05:42.453 --> 00:05:46.533
A 2028 passenger start still hangs on those tests and on policy.

00:05:47.293 --> 00:05:50.713
Tesla's service is already in multiple cities in Texas and Florida.

00:05:50.713 --> 00:05:56.333
The first cybercabs, with no steering wheel and no pedals, went into operation in Austin

00:05:56.333 --> 00:05:56.973
in September.

00:05:57.533 --> 00:06:02.573
The wider network still uses the model Y, so early growth does not wait on a dedicated

00:06:02.573 --> 00:06:03.433
factory line.

00:06:03.993 --> 00:06:09.773
Trading key calls Tesla's Edge vertical integration, manufacturing, driving software, charging,

00:06:10.053 --> 00:06:12.213
and the ride hailing platform in one company.

00:06:12.833 --> 00:06:18.673
The same piece says that if a cybercab can be built below $30,000, and if existing factories

00:06:18.673 --> 00:06:24.393
convert to Robotaxi production, the per vehicle cost could land well under Waymo's multi-sensor

00:06:24.393 --> 00:06:30.453
cars. That price is trading key's condition, not a Tesla figure in the article. Waymo's

00:06:30.453 --> 00:06:36.793
stack is geofence level 4, cameras, lidar, and millimeter wave radar, plus high-definition

00:06:36.793 --> 00:06:42.313
maps and remote operation. Every new city needs mapping, edge case checks, and talks with

00:06:42.313 --> 00:06:46.993
regulators, which trading key says slows the rollout and lifts hardware and operating

00:06:46.993 --> 00:06:53.153
cost. Tesla leans on a camera-heavy vision system and neural nets. Trading Key says cars

00:06:53.153 --> 00:06:58.393
without traditional controls face significant regulatory hurdles. Waymo can take an order

00:06:58.393 --> 00:07:03.533
in its own app or through Uber, depending on the city. Waymo's published comparison puts

00:07:03.533 --> 00:07:09.573
the rate of crashes with serious injury or death about 95% below human driving on the same roads.

00:07:10.253 --> 00:07:15.073
Trading Key also notes related research with lower rates in some pedestrian, cyclist,

00:07:15.073 --> 00:07:20.173
and intersection crashes, and says those results still have to be read with the operating area,

00:07:20.653 --> 00:07:26.333
the road types, and the method. Alphabet's company already has the paid rides, the city count,

00:07:26.553 --> 00:07:31.413
and a safety number regulators can read, and it pays with a slower city by city build.

00:07:32.033 --> 00:07:36.613
Tesla's side of the piece is the cheaper copy and a model Y fleet already on the road,

00:07:37.013 --> 00:07:42.033
against a thinner operating scale and an open question on cars that have no wheel and no pedals.

00:07:42.033 --> 00:07:49.553
The dated step in the article is still Toronto in 2028, and only if tests and local rules allow passengers then.

00:07:50.557 --> 00:07:57.897
On the calendar, Apple's three Paris Stores, Bordeaux St. Catherine, and Exxon Provence list Sunday hours from noon to 6,

00:07:58.417 --> 00:08:01.817
while Leal and Strasbourg stay shut Sunday and reopen Monday.

00:08:02.417 --> 00:08:06.197
Microsoft said Ignite for November 17th through the 21st.

00:08:06.197 --> 00:08:12.097
Prime Minister Anwar Ibrahim said Malaysia's security cannot be compromised, kept a partial

00:08:12.097 --> 00:08:15.677
ban on Google's ways and did not rule out wider limits.

00:08:16.157 --> 00:08:22.477
Google shipped Chrome OS 156 with Gemini talk to type dictation and video summaries on Chrome

00:08:22.477 --> 00:08:23.037
Book Plus.

00:08:23.497 --> 00:08:29.657
A report carried by 9-5 Macs as China's smartphone shipments fell 10% year-over-year in the third

00:08:29.657 --> 00:08:35.337
quarter, a 14-year low, with memory prices weighing on the market and Apple gaining ground.

00:08:35.337 --> 00:08:41.357
Apple TV subscribers in the United States can watch Formula One live in Dolby Atmos starting

00:08:41.357 --> 00:08:43.597
with this weekend's United States Grand Prix.

00:08:44.237 --> 00:08:49.657
Stefan Essert told Heizy there will not be an end-user tool, a proof-of-concept may follow,

00:08:50.057 --> 00:08:54.297
and most of those bugs are fixed in the coming iOS 27.2 update.

00:08:54.917 --> 00:09:00.477
Google Health 5.11 is rolling out this week for Fitbit trackers and the Pixel Watch, with

00:09:00.477 --> 00:09:03.197
Fitbit Air Health Guardian and Better Sleep Tracking.

00:09:03.197 --> 00:09:10.077
Purdue University, Northwest is giving first-year students Google Gemini licenses for artificial intelligence literacy.

00:09:10.927 --> 00:09:18.947
Apple ceded a second watch OS 27.2 release candidate, build 24 S-118, four days after the first.

00:09:19.467 --> 00:09:24.147
It adds Siri AI in French, Japanese, Korean, Portuguese, and Spanish.

00:09:24.667 --> 00:09:30.747
And Siri AI is not available in the EU or mainland China, with a public launch expected next week.

00:09:30.747 --> 00:09:36.710
Before we go, the court still has to decide how the Apple document fight moves, including

00:09:36.710 --> 00:09:38.610
whether newer records must be produced.

00:09:39.290 --> 00:09:41.030
That's Mag 7 Daily for today.

